</LINEAR_ISOTROPIC_MATERIALS>

#<NLMM142>
    ## Keyword: _NLMM142
    ## Properties of the NLMM125 material model
#    COUNT = 1 ; # N. of NLMM125 materials

    ## Content of each column:
    #  A -> Counter
    #  B -> Name of the material model
    #  C -> Mass per unit volume
    #  D -> Temperature coefficient
    #  E -> Poisson's coefficient
    #  F -> Young's modulus
    #  G -> Compressive strength
    #  H -> Strain at compression peak stress
    #  I -> Parameter defining the initial yield surface
    #  J -> Type of hardeding function after peak load
    #       - Available keywords: _CEB_FIP93 or _PERFECT_PLASTIC
    #  K -> Volume fraction of fibers (Vf)
    #
    #       Note: for plane concrete a Value of zero should be set for this parameter
    #
    #  L -> Aspect ratio of fibers (lf/Df)
    #  M -> Length efficiency factor of fibers
    #  N -> Orientation factor of fibers
    #  O -> Ultimate bond strength
    #  P -> Tensile strength
    #  Q -> Type of tensile-softening diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _TRILINEAR, _QUADRILINEAR or _CORNELISSEN
    #  R -> Ratio between the strain at the first post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  S -> Ratio between the stress at the first post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  T -> Ratio between the strain at the second post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  U -> Ratio between the stress at the second post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  V -> Ratio between the strain at the third post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  W -> Ratio between the stress at the third post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  X -> Mode I fracture energy (Gf)
    #  Y -> Type of mode I fracture energy update law
    #       - Available keywords: _NONE, _LINEAR, _QUADRATIC or _CUBIC
    #  Z -> Ultimate crack shear sliding (keyword or constant value)
    #       - Available keywords: _MAXIMUM_CRACKWIDTH
    #  AA -> Parameter to define the mode I fracture energy available to the new crack
    #  AB -> Type of shear-softening diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _NONE or _LINEAR
    #  AC -> Type of shear retention factor law (keyword or constant value)
    #       - Available keywords: _LINEAR, _QUADRATIC or _CUBIC
    #  AD -> Type of crack shear modelling appoach (used in shear retention model)
    #       - Available keywords: _INCREMENTAL or _TOTAL
    #  AE -> Crack shear strength
    #  AF -> Shear fracture energy (Gfs=GfII) (in nonlinear Mindlin shell: In-plane shear fracture energy)
    #  AG -> Type of unloading/reloading diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _SECANT or _ELASTIC
    #  AH -> Crack band width for the fracture mode I (keyword or constant value)
    #       - Available keywords: _SQRT_ELEMENT or _SQRT_IP
    #  AI -> Maximum n. of cracks
    #  AJ -> Threshold angle (degress)
    #
    #  Out-of-plane shear data:
    #    -> Used in nonlinear Mindlin shell
    #
    # AK -> Type of out-of-plane shear-softening diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _NONE, _LINEAR, _TRILINEAR or _CORNELISSEN
    # AL -> Minimum out-of-plane shear stress for softening behavior
    # AM -> Out-of-plane shear fracture energy
    # AN -> Ratio between the out-of-plane shear strain at the first
    #       post-peak point and the ultimate out-of-plane shear strain
    #       trilinear out-of-plane shear-softening diagram
    # AO -> Ratio between the out-of-plane shear stress at the first
    #       post-peak point and the out-of-plane shear strength of the
    #       trilinear out-of-plane shear-softening diagram
    # AP -> Ratio between the out-of-plane shear strain at the second
    #       post-peak point and the ultimate out-of-plane shear strain
    #       of the trilinear out-of-plane shear-softening diagram
    # AQ -> Ratio between the out-of-plane shear stress at the second
    #       post-peak point and the out-of-plane shear strength of the
    #       trilinear out-of-plane shear-softening diagram
    #  A  B                C           D            E           F
#    1  TEST01   2.50e-005    1.0e-005          0.2        2.7000e+004
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    #  G           H           I           J                     K           L
#    30.00      0.0017         0.4           _PERFECT_PLASTIC   0.00       54.55
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    #  M            N           O           P           Q                       R           S
#    0.5          0.25        6.50         2.45           _TRILINEAR       0.2         0.70
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # T            U          V          W           X           Y
#    0.75         0.2        0.0        0.0         0.12           _NONE
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # Z                            AA           AB           AC           AD
#    _MAXIMUM_CRACKWIDTH             2           _NONE      _QUADRATIC         _INCREMENTAL
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # AE            AF           AG           AH              AI            AJ       AK
#    1.6           0.3           _SECANT      _SQRT_IP         2          30.0       _NONE
    #-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    #   AL            AM           AN           AO              AP            AQ
#    0.0           3.0           0.13        0.5            0.22          0.15 ;
    #Gfc=15
#  </NLMM142>

  <NLMM111>
    ## Keyword: _NLMM111
    ## Properties of the NLMM111 material model
    COUNT = 1 ; # N. of NLMM111 materials

    ## MY_GROUPtent of each column:
    #  A -> Counter
    #  B -> Name of the material model
    #  C -> Mass per unit volume
    #  D -> Temperature coefficient
    #  E -> Poisson's coefficient
    #  F -> Young's modulus
    #  G -> Compressive strength
    #  H -> Tensile strength
    #  I -> Type of tensile-softening diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _TRILINEAR, _QUADRILINEAR or _CORNELISSEN
    #  J -> Ratio between the strain at the first post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  K -> Ratio between the stress at the first post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  L -> Ratio between the strain at the seMY_GROUPd post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  M -> Ratio between the stress at the seMY_GROUPd post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the trilinear/quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  N -> Ratio between the strain at the third post-peak point and the
    #       ultimate strain of the quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  O -> Ratio between the stress at the third post-peak point and the
    #       tensile strength of the quadrilinear tensile-softening diagram (fracture mode I)
    #  P -> Mode I fracture energy (Gf)
    #  Q -> Parameter to define the mode I fracture energy available to the new crack
    #  R -> Type of shear-softening diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _NONE, _LINEAR, _TRILINEAR or _CORNELISSEN
    #  S -> Ratio between the (shear strain minus peak shear strain) at the first post-peak point and
    #       the (ultimate shear strain minus peak shear strain) of the trilinear shear-softening diagram
    #  T -> Ratio between the the shear stress at the first post-peak point and the
    #       shear strength of the trilinear shear-softening diagram
    #  U -> Ratio between the (shear strain minus peak shear strain) at the second post-peak point and
    #       the (ultimate shear strain minus peak shear strain) of the trilinear shear-softening diagram
    #  V -> Ratio between the the shear stress at the seMY_GROUPd post-peak point and the
    #       shear strength of the trilinear shear-softening diagram
    #  W -> Type of shear retention factor law (keyword or costant value)
    #       - Available keywords: _LINEAR, _QUADRATIC or _CUBIC
    #  X -> Type of crack shear modelling appoach (used in shear retention model)
    #       - Available keywords: _INCREMENTAL or _TOTAL
    #  Y -> Crack shear strength
    #  Z -> Shear fracture energy (Gfs=GfII=GfIII)
    # AA -> Type of unloading/reloading diagram
    #       - Available keywords: _SECANT or _ELASTIC
    # AB -> Crack band width for the fracture mode I (keyword or MY_GROUPstant value)
    #       - Available keywords: _SQRT_ELEMENT or _SQRT_IP
    # AC -> Maximum n. of cracks
    # AD -> Threshold angle (degress)


    # A		   B	     C			      D		        	E		          F	         G
    1			TEST01 	2.50E-06		 1e-005		      0.15       	 27000.0   	   60.0
